markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Using AI Tools

AI can help teachers save time on planning, feedback, and administrative tasks. But deciding when and how to use AI is just as important as knowing what it can do.

A helpful way to approach AI use is to pause and **THINK** before using it:

<div style="width:80%; max-width:900px; margin:0 auto; font-family:ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica, Arial; color:#292F36;">

<div style="border:1px solid #D9DDE3; border-radius:16px; overflow:hidden; background:#FFFFFF; box-shadow:0 4px 12px rgba(41,47,54,0.06);">

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
T
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Task & Purpose</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Start with a clear reason for using AI. Use AI when it helps achieve a specific learning, instructional, or professional goal. Choose AI because it improves the process or outcome, not simply because it is available.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
H
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Human Oversight</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Always review and refine AI-generated content. Check for accuracy, clarity, and bias before sharing with students.</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
I
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Instructional Quality</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Keep quality at the center of your decisions. Check that AI-generated materials are accurate, aligned to standards, and appropriate for your students.
</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr; border-bottom:1px solid #E8ECF0;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
N
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">No Sensitive Data</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
Protect student privacy when using AI tools. Avoid sharing personal or sensitive information, and follow your school's or district's AI policies.</div>
</div>
</div>

<!-- ROW -->
<div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: 80px 1fr;">
<div style="background:#8C52BA; color:#FFFFFF; font-weight:800; font-size:28px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center;">
K
</div>
<div style="padding:16px;">
<div style="font-weight:800; font-size:18px; margin-bottom:6px;">Keep Professional Judgment First</div>
<div style="font-size:15px; line-height:1.5;">
AI is a tool, not a replacement for your expertise. AI does not know your students, classroom context, or instructional goals, so your judgment is essential</div>
</div>
</div>

</div>
</div>

<br>

In Module 5, Ensuring a Responsible Approach, you'll explore data privacy, responsible AI use, and other important considerations in greater depth.
MARKDOWN
